<title>ITALY: San Paolo 1H cons net profit up 33.7 pct.</title>
<headline>San Paolo 1H cons net profit up 33.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Consolidated net profit   321  vs  up 33.7 percent</p>
<p>    Parent net profit	  287   vs  up 10.4 percent</p>
<p>    Profit-equity ratio    3.3 pct vs  2.75 pct</p>
<p>    Net profit per share     up 22 percent</p>
<p>    Net interest income    1,931   vs  down 3.3 percent</p>
<p>    Non-interest income	494   vs  up 153 percent</p>
<p>    Net operating profit     997   vs  up 6.1 percent</p>
<p>    Client loans	 98 trillion vs down 2.8 percent</p>
<p>Client deposits 128.5 trillion vs up 2.4 percent</p>
<p>NOTE - Italy's largest banking group Istituto Bancario San Paolo di Torino said its parent group results came after the merger with Crediop and Banca Nazionale delle Comunicazioni, and the demerger of the &quot;new Crediop&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129450</p>
</text>
